---
smd: 1
title: Pipes in table cells
summary: Pins how a `|` reads in a table cell, as on GitHub, so later releases are compared against it. An escaped pipe stays in its cell; one in a code span still splits the cell.
status: draft
updated: 2026-10-15
---

## Escaped pipes

| Operator | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `a \|\| b` | Either one |
| `x \| y` | A union type |
| A \| B | Text with a pipe |

## A pipe in a code span

| Command | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `grep a | wc -l` | Count the matches |

Outside a table, `a | b` is a code span as written.
